who are severely emotionally disturbed</source><year>1989</year><publisher-name>Washington, DC, National Technical Assistance Center for Children's Mental Health, Georgetwon University Child Development Center</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carrillo</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Green</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Bethancourt</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cross-cultural primary care: A patient-based approach</article-title><source>Annals of Internal Medicine</source><year>1999</year><volume>130</volume><fpage>829</fpage><lpage>834</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10366373</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Culhane-Pera</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Reif</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Egli</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Baker</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kassekert</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A curriculum for multicultural education in family medicine</article-title><source>Family Medicine</source><year>2006</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>719</fpage><lpage>723</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9397362</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kristal</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Pennock</surname><given-names>PW</given-names></name><name><surname>Foote</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Trygstad</surname><given-names>CW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cross-cultural family medicine residency training</article-title><source>Journal of Family Practice</